%!testlib
% The even-odd interior of a fill or clip is resolved over the rows the
% device holds, not the rows the subject reaches, run through
% `xpost -q --no-sandbox -d null` by run-ps-test.sh.
%
% A subject reaching far above or below the page -- a program sizes its
% bounding box -- covers no pixel there, so its interior is resolved over
% the page's rows and no others. Resolving it over the subject's rows
% instead walked a boundary the program made as tall as it liked, so an
% eofill or eoclip of such a subject ran the row walk without end; bounded
% to the page, it completes.
{ << /PageSize [500 500] >> setpagedevice
  newpath 10 10 moveto 490 10 lineto 250 100000000 lineto closepath
  100 100 moveto 400 100 lineto 250 100000000 lineto closepath
  eofill }
    (an eofill of a subject reaching far off the page completes) works
{ << /PageSize [500 500] >> setpagedevice
  newpath 10 10 moveto 490 10 lineto 250 100000000 lineto closepath
  eoclip 0 0 500 500 rectfill }
    (an eoclip of a subject reaching far off the page completes) works
% an ordinary on-page even-odd fill is untouched
{ << /PageSize [500 500] >> setpagedevice
  newpath 50 50 moveto 450 50 lineto 250 450 lineto closepath
  150 150 moveto 350 150 lineto 250 350 lineto closepath eofill }
    (an ordinary even-odd fill still fills) works
verdict
